description: Cursor-specific reminders for shared UCA Kit engineering instructions
alwaysApply: true
---

Use root `AGENTS.md`, `.agents/AGENTS.md`, `AGENT-SKILL-MAP.md`, and `HOST-CAPABILITY-FALLBACK.md` as the source of truth; keep this adapter short and non-conflicting.

Before substantial work, select relevant skills up front, then actually read the selected `.agents/skills/<name>/SKILL.md` files. Do not load the whole skill catalog or assume a file was loaded merely because it exists.

Cursor can automatically delegate to project subagents under `.cursor/agents/` when task complexity, context and the subagent descriptions justify it. Use `designer` for meaningful user-facing design work and `service-strategist` for business/service-offering planning; combine these for a joint design + service plan. Don't invoke unrelated agents on simple tasks. If Cursor does not expose or invoke subagents in the active session, carry the work out sequentially as the lead and say that delegation was unavailable.

For usage, use a host-supported local budget integration only if it is available and verified. Never claim the OpenCode plugin works in Cursor; the included usage ledger can be used manually unless a tested Cursor-specific hook/plugin is added. Never store or transmit prompts/code for UCA Kit telemetry.
